#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:7
msgid ""
"Mattermost system admins using Mattermost Cloud or Mattermost Server can "
"use Advanced Permissions to customize which users can perform specific "
"actions, such as creating teams, managing channels, and configuring "
"webhooks. The Mattermost permission system is based on a modified RBAC "
"(role-based access control) architecture, using roles to determine which "
"users have the ability to perform various actions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:9
msgid "Two permission schemes are provided in Mattermost:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:11
msgid ""
"**System Scheme**: Applies permissions universally across all teams and "
"channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:12
msgid ""
"**Team Override Schemes**: Allow admins to customize permissions for each"
" team."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:14
msgid ""
"This document describes the types of permissions that can be given to "
"users of Mattermost using schemes as well as channel settings and roles. "
"The :doc:`permissions backend documentation </administration-"
"guide/onboard/advanced-permissions-backend-infrastructure>` provides "
"additional technical details around permissions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:17
msgid "Permissions structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:19
msgid ""
"The Mattermost System Console provides a number of elements for Admins to"
" control the permissions in their system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:22
msgid "System scheme"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:24
msgid ""
"You can set the default permissions granted to system admins, team "
"admins, channel admins, guests (if enabled), and all members. The "
"permissions granted in the System Scheme apply system-wide, meaning:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:26
msgid ""
"**Guests:** If Guest Accounts are enabled, permissions apply to guest "
"users in all channels, in all teams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:27
msgid ""
"**All Members:** Permissions apply to all members, including admins, in "
"all channels, in all teams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:28
msgid ""
"**Channel Administrators:** Permissions apply to all channel admins in "
"all channels, in all teams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:29
msgid ""
"**Team Administrators:** Permissions apply to all team admins, in all "
"teams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:31
msgid ""
"To override the System Scheme default permissions in a specific team, you"
" must set up a Team Override Scheme."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:33
msgid ""
"You can access the System Scheme interface by going to **System Console >"
" User Management > Permissions > System Scheme**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:38
msgid "Team override scheme"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/_static/badges/entry-adv.rst:7
msgid ""
"|plans-img-yellow| Available on `Entry and Enterprise Advanced "
"<https://mattermost.com/pricing/>`__ plans"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:43
msgid ""
"On systems with multiple :ref:`Mattermost teams <end-user-"
"guide/collaborate/organize-using-teams:single team versus multiple "
"teams>`, each team may operate and collaborate in a unique way. Team "
"Override Schemes give Admins the flexibility to tailor permissions to the"
" needs of each team."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:45
msgid "When you use this permission scheme:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:47
msgid ""
"The permissions granted in a Team Override Scheme apply only in the teams"
" which are assigned to the scheme."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:48
msgid ""
"The System Scheme does not apply to teams that are added to a Team "
"Override Scheme."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:49
msgid "Teams can only belong to one Team Override Scheme."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions.rst:51
msgid ""
"You can access the Team Override Scheme interface by going to **System "
"Console > User Management > Permissions > Team Override Schemes**."
msgstr ""

